<title>JAPAN: Mazda Sept domestic output up 5.6% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Mazda Sept domestic output up 5.6% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp said on Friday its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in September were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	   67,104   up    5.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		52,727   up    3.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; Buses  14,377   up   12.0 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     35,051   down  5.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		22,361   up    6.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; Buses  12,690   down 21.3 percent</p>
<p> Exports		43,226   down  9.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		34,777   down 18.1 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	8,449   up   59.1 percent</p>
<p>Mazda's domestic vehicle production rebounded in September after falling the month before, helped by strong domestic demand for its new Demio compact wagon model.</p>
<p>Its domestic sales fell for the second straight month year-on-year, mainly due to slow demand for its trucks and 660cc minivehicles. But sales of passenger cars rose 20.8 percent.</p>
<p>Mazda's vehicle exports fell for the second straight month due to slow demand in North America and Europe.</p>
</text>
